  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer planar dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45° incidence using TiO2 (high index) and SiO2 (low index) in alternating sequence. Layer 1 (incident side) is TiO2, layer 24 (substrate side) is SiO2. Initialize 40% of the optimization population with the exact thickness sequence from iteration 25 best candidate: [31.71, 83.18, 96.27, 118.44, 47.59, 92.97, 82.44, 107.21, 60.11, 97.03, 70.18, 111.24, 55.68, 105.93, 54.09, 83.96, 40.44, 75.39, 48.57, 96.17, 58.55, 96.31, 36.29, 151.03] nm. For remaining 60% of population, initialize with random thicknesses clipped to [70, 130] nm window. During gradient-based optimization, constrain thickness mutation amplitude to ±8 nm per iteration. Evaluate performance at 45° incidence for unpolarized light (average of s and p polarization). Score based on: high reflectance in 450-650 nm band, high transmittance in 700-1000 nm band, suppressed transmittance in 450-650 nm band, suppressed reflectance in 700-1000 nm band. Maximum layer count: 24. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dichroic filter on fused silica at 45° incidence. Maximize mean reflectance in 450–650 nm and mean transmittance in 700–1000 nm while minimizing cross-band leakage. Constrain thicknesses to [30, 160] nm with ±8 nm mutation limits during gradient-based search.",
